        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1377499587,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "The fruit is made into both preserves and cider. Pehr Kalm, a disciple of 18-century botanist Carl Linnaeus, wrote of the fruit:\n\nThe apples, or crabs, are small, sour and unfit for anything but to make vinegar of. They lie under the trees all winter and acquire a yellow color. They seldom begin to rot before spring comes on.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "es": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (es): Malus coronaria § Usos",
        "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malus_coronaria#Usos",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 146220220,
        "heading": "Usos",
        "text": "Aunque comestibles, al ser sus frutos de sabor más agrio, el fruto se prefiere utilizar en preparaciones tales como conservas y en sidra.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
